.TH RESOLVE-READY 1 "2026-11-08" "Resolve Ready 1.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
resolve-ready \- convert video for DaVinci Resolve on Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B resolve-ready
.RI [ FILE ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B resolve-ready
is a small GTK 4 application that transcodes footage into formats
DaVinci Resolve can edit on Linux.  It converts video to DNxHR or ProRes
and audio to 24-bit PCM at 48 kHz, writes a
.B .mov
file, verifies the result, and keeps the original media.
.PP
When started without arguments it opens a window where files and folders
can be dragged in.  File and folder arguments are added to the conversion
queue on startup.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the application version and exit without starting GTK.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show the command-line options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/resolve-ready/settings.json
User preferences and the last-used output folder.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR ffprobe (1)
.PP
Project home page: https://github.com/mdshakibsami/resolve-ready
